WEBVTT

00:00:56.594 --> 00:01:00.139
even if it's not actually enjoyable,
and, in fact, a waste of time.

00:01:00.181 --> 00:01:05.061
So for example, we scroll
through social media "for fun,"

00:01:05.103 --> 00:01:10.066
even though doing so often makes us feel
bad about, like, kind of everything.

00:01:10.066 --> 00:01:14.320
Or we'll say, "That was so fun.
We should do that again soon" --

00:01:14.362 --> 00:01:17.448
(Laughter)

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.784
... in response to things
that weren't that fun

00:01:19.784 --> 00:01:22.954
and that we don't want to do again, ever.

00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:24.997
(Laughter)

00:01:25.039 --> 00:01:27.875
But it's not really our fault
that we're a little bit sloppy

00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:29.502
about how we use the word "fun,"

00:01:29.544 --> 00:01:32.171
because even the dictionary
doesn't get it quite right.